{"criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Accomplished","mark":8,"evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching"},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Reef-monitoring satellites could also be used to report sea surface temperatures, thermal stress on coral, and bathymetry"}],"reasoning":"Mission concept, users, and national need for Great Barrier Reef monitoring are clearly defined and referenced. Technical specifications and quantitative requirements could be more thoroughly detailed."},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":5,"evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km"}],"reasoning":"A Gantt chart is included and mapped out. However, the plan lacks risk/contingency considerations, planned future information sources are not listed, and orbital physics logic is flawed."},{"id":"C3","level":"Deficient","mark":2,"evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}],"reasoning":"No actual preliminary mission design results, hand calculations, or STK outputs are presented beyond completing general tutorials."},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6,"evidence":[{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"¹ https://www.noaa.gov/education/resource-collections/ocean-coasts/ocean-acidification"}],"reasoning":"The report is clearly structured, readable, and includes a well-formatted Gantt chart. However, footnotes are raw URLs without full bibliographic details, and figures lack formal captions."}],"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R5","met":"no","where":null},{"id":"R6","met":"no","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"A geostationary orbit cannot physically exist at an altitude of 600 km (geostationary altitude is ~35,786 km above the equator). A 600 km orbit is Low Earth Orbit (LEO) with a ~96-minute period."}],"overall":"Good mission rationale for Australia. However, preliminary technical work is missing, planned information sources are absent, and asserting a 600 km geostationary orbit represents a major orbital mechanics error."}
